========== SUPERIEUR (summarized) ==========
- [extract-constant] \\int cf\\,dx = c\\int f\\,dx
  \\begin{aligned} & \\textcolor{blue}{\\int \\dfrac{x}{4}\\,dx} \\\\ & = \\dfrac{1}{4} \\dfrac{x^2}{2} \\end{aligned}
  - [apply-power-rule] \\int x^n\\,dx = \\dfrac{x^{n+1}}{n+1}
    \\begin{aligned} & \\textcolor{blue}{\\int x\\,dx} \\\\ & = \\dfrac{x^2}{2} \\end{aligned}
Antiderivative: \\dfrac{1}{4} \\dfrac{x^2}{2}

========== SUPERIEUR (detailed) ==========
- [extract-constant] \\int cf\\,dx = c\\int f\\,dx
  · Une constante multiplicative sort de l'intégrale : ∫\\dfrac{1}{4}·f(x) dx = \\dfrac{1}{4}·∫f(x) dx.
  \\begin{aligned} & \\textcolor{blue}{\\int \\dfrac{x}{4}\\,dx} \\\\ & = \\dfrac{1}{4} \\dfrac{x^2}{2} \\end{aligned}
  - [apply-power-rule] \\int x^n\\,dx = \\dfrac{x^{n+1}}{n+1}
    · (x^n)' = n·x^(n-1), donc ∫x^n dx = \\dfrac{x^{n+1}}{n+1} avec n = 1 (et n ≠ -1).
    \\begin{aligned} & \\textcolor{blue}{\\int x\\,dx} \\\\ & = \\dfrac{x^2}{2} \\end{aligned}
Antiderivative: \\dfrac{1}{4} \\dfrac{x^2}{2}
"
`;

